# QuantLLMBot Research-and-Evidence Gate

Before changing trading behavior, architecture, prompts, regime interpretation,
entries, levels, risk, exits, targets, or protection, perform a read-only R&D
pass first. State the proposed hypothesis, affected decision path, expected
benefit, possible harm, and falsification test before editing.

A behavioral change may proceed only when at least one evidence route qualifies:

1. Broker-authoritative or leakage-safe replay evidence supports it across
   multiple complete trading days and relevant sessions/regimes; one trade,
   one day, screenshots, anecdotes, or gross P&L alone do not qualify.
2. A directly relevant trading book or existing approved corpus principle
   supports it, with instrument/timeframe limitations made explicit.
3. At least two independent credible internet sources support it; prefer
   primary/authoritative sources and record material disagreement.

Books and internet evidence justify a hypothesis, not profitability. Validate
material expectancy claims on XAUUSD data before calling them improvements.
Never infer causation from post-change profit alone.

If none of the three routes qualifies, veto the behavioral change: do not edit,
activate, tune, or work around the gate. Report the missing evidence and the
minimum experiment or data needed to reconsider it.

Pure software-correctness, security, observability, or data-integrity fixes may
use reproducible code, test, broker, or log evidence instead of trading books,
but must preserve trading semantics unless a behavioral route above qualifies.

Keep deterministic components factual and safety-oriented. They may calculate,
validate, enforce broker/risk invariants, and protect against latency-sensitive
sudden moves. They must not replace Qwen's ordinary market-structure judgment
unless the protected V2 architecture is explicitly changed after this gate.

Record supporting and contradicting evidence near the change, update only
`XAUUSD_SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE_V2.md` for architecture, and verify with focused
tests plus replay proportional to behavioral risk. Do not restart live services
or activate a qualified change until activation is explicitly in scope.
